# Docs (strict)

Wrap prose at ~80 columns (commit bodies at 72). Use the same tone as `README.md` and `docs/architecture.md`: short sentences, no hype, no git jargon unless the reader is in an engine/ADR doc.

## Where

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| User-visible behavior | `README.md` capabilities + `CHANGELOG.md` |
| Layer / git / cache / IPC | `docs/architecture.md` |
| A rejected alternative or a new boundary | new ADR in `docs/decisions/` |
| How to run / test / PR | `CONTRIBUTING.md` |

Do not add a second architecture doc, a wiki, or a `docs/spec.md`. Do not duplicate ADRs into README.

## ADRs

Next number after the last `docs/decisions/NNNN-*.md`. Kebab filename. House template:

```markdown
# ADR-NNNN: Title

**Status:** accepted
**Date:** YYYY-MM-DD

## Context
## Decision
## Consequences
```

Status is `accepted`, `superseded`, or `rejected`. Link the sibling ADR if superseded.

## Changelog

Keep a Changelog headings (`Added` / `Changed` / `Fixed`). Past tense. User-facing only — no "refactored cache mutex" entries.
